Farming Robot Website — Complete Feature Explanation
Your idea is to control your existing Arduino Uno farming robot through a website that works on phones, Windows computers, Ubuntu and tablets. The website sends commands through a hosted backend and a Bluetooth bridge running on a nearby computer.

Here is how each feature is intended to work, including the manual controls, voice commands, sensors, and background operation.
1. Manual Control
This section lets you control the robot yourself using on-screen buttons or a computer keyboard.
